---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A snackbar is a brief, transient message at the bottom of the screen. It hides itself after
  <code>duration</code> milliseconds (4000 by default); the timer pauses while the pointer is over it or
  focus is inside it. A snackbar with an action, or with <code>duration='0'</code>, stays until it is
  closed, so there is time to reach the action. Opening one snackbar closes the one before; to show several
  at once use <a href='/components/notification-manager'><code>wc-notification-manager</code></a>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button id='show-basic'>Show snackbar</wc-button>
  <wc-button id='show-action'>Show action</wc-button>
  <br />

  <wc-snackbar id='basic-snackbar' message='Message archived' duration='3500'></wc-snackbar>
  <wc-snackbar id='action-snackbar' intent='danger' multiline action-label='Retry' dismissible>
    Unable to save changes. Check your connection and try again.
  </wc-snackbar>

  <p id='snackbar-log' class='text-body'> </p>

  <script is:inline>
    const basic = document.querySelector('#basic-snackbar');
    const action = document.querySelector('#action-snackbar');
    const log = document.querySelector('#snackbar-log');

    function updateLog(message) {
      log.textContent = message;
    }

    document.querySelector('#show-basic').addEventListener('click', () => {
      basic.show();
      updateLog('Showing basic snackbar');
    });

    document.querySelector('#show-action').addEventListener('click', () => {
      action.show();
      updateLog('Showing snackbar with action');
    });

    basic.addEventListener('close', event => {
      updateLog(`Basic snackbar closed (${event.detail.reason})`);
    });

    action.addEventListener('action', () => {
      updateLog('Retry clicked');
    });

    action.addEventListener('close', event => {
      updateLog(`Action snackbar closed (${event.detail.reason})`);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Intents</h3>

<p>
  <code>intent</code> (<code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code>)
  adds a matching icon, and a hidden label that screen readers read before the message.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-snackbar preview intent='info' message='A new version is available.'></wc-snackbar>
  <wc-snackbar preview intent='success' message='Message sent.'></wc-snackbar>
  <wc-snackbar preview intent='warning' message='You are offline.'></wc-snackbar>
  <wc-snackbar preview intent='danger' message='Upload failed.' action-label='Retry'></wc-snackbar>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>

<p>
  A snackbar is a polite live region (<code>role="status"</code>); <code>intent='danger'</code> makes it
  assertive (<code>role="alert"</code>). <code>dismissible</code> shows a close button and lets Escape close
  the snackbar while focus is inside it.
</p>

<h3>Events</h3>

<p>
  <code>open</code> fires when it opens. <code>close</code> fires when it starts to close, with
  <code>detail.reason</code>: <code>'timeout'</code>, <code>'action'</code> (the action or close button),
  <code>'escape'</code>, or <code>'api'</code> (<code>hide()</code>, <code>open = false</code>, or another
  snackbar opening). <code>action</code> fires when the action button is pressed.
</p>
